From 790715c27dff83838a456add85160a3b60eb93b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:57:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] media: camss: csid: add the 980 generation and report
 frame starts from CSID

The CSID found on SM8750 (call it generation 980) moves the capture
interrupts from the VFE to the CSID: the VFE of that generation has no
useful interrupt sources, and the CSID reports RDI buffer done, register
update completion and CAMIF start-of-frame per CSI2 stream instead.

Add camss-csid-980.c with the register maps for both the full and the
lite variants.  The full variant splits the register update into
separate RUP and AUP commands that need an extra trigger write, while
the lite variant keeps the combined RUP/AUP command of the previous
generations, so struct csid_device gains dedicated rup_update and
aup_update fields next to the existing combined reg_update.

A buffer is only complete once its frame started, and the sequence
number of a frame is defined by its start: turn the CSID SOF interrupt
into the frame start source.  camss_frame_start() forwards it to the
paired VFE, which raises V4L2_EVENT_FRAME_SYNC on the video node,
increments the sequence only there, and marks buffers done before their
frame started as erroneous.  Hardware generations that still report
frame starts through the VFE keep the previous behaviour, as the new
vfe_hw_ops callback is only provided by VFE implementations that need
it.

Signed-off-by: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
